{title: Little Sun}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{start_of_verse}
My little sun is asleep, curled up like a kitten.
The quiet whisper of the clock seems to echo the steps.
My soul is so warm and so calm. Wrapped up
In a blanket of care and bright dreams.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
strong and brave, then like a white swan,
fragile and tender, a boundless swallow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Time will dissolve the days, the minutes gone by,
The lights of bright colours and the trace of hardships.
What will memory leave us? Which moments?
We choose them ourselves, and we shape them ourselves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Breathe in, and a pink curl flows down.
Breathe out, and a spark of a light smile flashed.
My soul is so warm and, as if on wings,
The depth of grey eyes carries me away.
{end_of_verse}
